# Claude Code runtime state under .claude/ — per-machine, per-session, rewritten
# constantly (scheduled_tasks.lock is a PID + session id). Claude Code declares these
# in .git/info/exclude, but that file is LOCAL: never committed, never cloned. So a
# fresh clone has no protection, and one `git add -A` commits them.
#
# That matters more here than elsewhere because .claude/ is a framework subtree prefix
# and is hash-checked: a committed lock file is either unclassified (framework:verify
# --check fails in CI) or, if someone "fixes" that by declaring it framework-owned,
# churns on every session and produces a permanent false "framework file modified" in
# every portal. Mirrored in platform/framework.json's ownership.ignored as well.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
.claude/routines/.state/
.claude/checkpoints/
.claude/mailbox/
.claude/agent-registry.json
.claude/agent-memory-local
.claude/first-run
.claude/assistant-daemon-state.json

# Supabase CLI scratch state — was tracked by accident; never belongs in the repo
supabase/.temp/

# CodeGraph index — per-machine, regenerated by `codegraph index`. The directory
# self-ignores its own contents (`*` plus `!.gitignore`), but NOT the .gitignore it
# ships, so without this line a `git add -A` commits .codegraph/.gitignore as a
# tracked file with no declared owner, and framework:verify --check fails in CI.
.codegraph/
